            "download_url": "https://www.blenderkit.com/api/v1/downloads/133565/",
            "tooltip": "Merkurs X-3\n\nYes, another one. Merkurs X-3 was based\n from we all familiar with. That is,\n Ford GT. Merkurs X-3 is a mid sized\n two door supercar that has a mid rear\n engine and all wheel drive layout to\n maximize grip on all four tyre. The\n lightweight body of carbon fiber.\n Aluminum structures able to minimize\n the weight of the high strength\n subframe.\n\nWith long suspension and inboard\n damper we able to deliver track\n capable vehicle dynamic. To help\n overall performance. It was equipped\n with carbon ceramic brakes that we\n have designed into Merkurs X-3. Lastly\n, it was powered with twin turbocharged\n, intercooled 3.5 liter V6 and produce\n up to 665 horsepower.\n\nThe teardrop shape of the Merkurs X-3\n is the result of extensive check in\n the simulated wind tunnel to minimize\n aerodynamic drag, maximize aerodynamic\n stability at high speed, cornering and\n others. But nonetheless, whether on\n the road or on the track, every single\n element of the Merkurs X-3 was\n designed to deliver the extraordinary\n speed and exceptional handling found\n only in purpose built racing cars.\n\nCurrently, project has been completed\n with detailed dashboard and cockpit.\n But nonetheless, this project actually\n meant to be a modification for assetto\n corsa. At least that's the plan.\n Anyway, let's see about that. oh yea,\n there's animation i set for the door.\n atleast for BlenderKit user. Frame 0 -\n 250. Just reverse or flip the keyframe\n for closing animation. that's it from\n me. Any questions or issue, Feel free\n to contact us.\n\nEmail: mohdallathif2002@gmail\n.com\n\nStatus: Completed\n\nRelease Date: 30 /\n 07 / 2022 (BlenderKit)\n\nsize: 2.21m, 5.21m, 1.16m\nface count: 462751, render: 462751\nfiles size: 26MB 296KB\ntex resolution: 4 - 3108\nlicense: royalty_free\n",
